// Live routing cases — one JSON object per line, this deployment's own catalog.
//
// Written in the USER's voice, not the catalog's: the eval flags a case whose query reuses
// its target agent's own description, because such a case passes under a broken router too.
// Most cases carry an `acceptable` SET, since several specialists are often defensible and
// demanding one exact name measures the labeller's taste rather than the routing.
//
// Run: pnpm routing:eval -- --mode live            (add --triage, then --second-pass)
// Run it where the RERANKER is reachable — see README.md. A workstation run scores a
// different pipeline for per-probe ranks.
{"id":"live-device-url-spinner","query":"https://intern.firmanetz.de/freigaben dreht bei mir seit heute nur den ladekreisel, kannst du mal gucken ob da ueberhaupt noch was nachkommt?","language":"de","note":"A JS-rendered page that never finishes loading needs an agent that navigates, waits and looks again, which only browser_agent can do; researcher is the tempting wrong answer because the query hands over a URL, but a plain fetch returns the empty shell, i.e. exactly the symptom being reported, and ops_triage is out because the user asks what the page still shows, not why a named service is unhealthy - no service is named at all.","expect":{"acceptable":["browser_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["device","url","bare-question","cross-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-device-internal-webui-import","query":"auf dem testserver laeuft ne weboberflaeche auf port 3000, mach die mal auf und sag mir ob der import von gestern nacht durchgelaufen ist","language":"de","note":"Opening a web UI and reading a status off it is browser_agent even when that UI sits on an internal host; api_integrator is the tempting wrong answer because host-plus-port reads as an endpoint, but the user asks for a page to be opened and read rather than a response body validated, and computer_use_agent is deliberately NOT listed because nothing in the query says the port is reachable only from that machine's own desktop - assuming it would be padding.","expect":{"acceptable":["browser_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["device","imperative","two-part","cross-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-device-stuck-dialog","query":"auf dem rechner im keller haengt seit gestern so ein fenster mit ner fehlermeldung fest, was steht da drin?","language":"de","note":"The evidence exists only as pixels on a named remote machine's screen, so the desktop driver is the only agent that can read it; ops_triage and log_analyst are the tempting wrong answers because 'haengt seit gestern' is incident phrasing, but a modal box sitting on a desktop is in no log file and behind no health endpoint.","expect":{"acceptable":["computer_use_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["device","bare-question","cross-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-device-reattach-session","query":"here's the id from earlier: sess-7c41 - get back onto that box and tell me whether the export that was running there is done","language":"en","note":"A pasted session id plus 'get back onto that box' is a reattach to an existing desktop session, which only computer_use_agent can do, and the anaphora resolves inside the query (the box is sess-7c41, the export is the one running there); ops_triage is the tempting wrong answer for 'is it done', but the answer is a progress window on that machine, not a probe result.","expect":{"acceptable":["computer_use_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["device","pasted","follow-up","imperative"]}
{"id":"live-device-cert-bound-tool","query":"that old tool only works in the browser on my work laptop because the certificate sits there - can you get on it and check whether my request went through?","language":"en","note":"The one genuine boundary case in the cluster: it is a browser flow, but a client certificate binds it to one physical machine, so driving that laptop's desktop is exactly as defensible as opening a fresh browser session, and the case exists to see which of the two surface signals the router weighs harder; vision_browser_analyst stays out because nothing has been captured yet and it drives nothing.","expect":{"acceptable":["browser_agent","computer_use_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["device","boundary","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-data-xlsx-monatssumme","query":"in der xlsx liegen alle bestellungen vom letzten jahr, rechne mir bitte pro monat die summe aus","language":"de","note":"A file that already sits in the workspace plus a group-by month with a sum is data_analyst's core work; document_intake is the close call because it also opens XLSX, but the user does not want the sheet turned into readable content, they want figures computed, and nothing here points at a live DB (sql_specialist) or at a picture (chart_designer). The one catalog word in the query, 'xlsx', is a tag on data_analyst AND on document_intake, so it does not decide the case for the target.","expect":{"acceptable":["data_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["data","imperative","file-reference","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-data-zeilen-klemmen","query":"hab dir die datei hochgeladen, jede zeile ein aufruf mit dauer und statuscode - wo klemmt es?","language":"de","note":"Genuine boundary inside the cluster: one row per request with a duration and a status code is an access log, which is log_analyst's home turf (latency outliers, 4xx/5xx clusters), but it is also a plain tabular file, so data_analyst computing percentiles and a group-by status is equally defensible; the query never says the word log, so whichever wins is a routing decision and not a lexical one. Zero shared tokens with either target.","expect":{"acceptable":["log_analyst","data_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["data","pasted-artifact","boundary-in-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-data-report-vs-db","query":"the monthly report i exported doesn't match what the database says - find out which rows are missing","language":"en","note":"Boundary inside the cluster: reconciling an export against the live system it came from needs both halves, so sql_specialist (query the real tables) and data_analyst (read the export and diff it) are both defensible entry points and picking one would be taste; evidence_analyst is the wrong shape because the conflict is between rows of structured data, not between prose sources. 'database' and 'exported' are unavoidable - they name the two inputs, which is the axis this whole cluster turns on.","expect":{"acceptable":["sql_specialist","data_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["data","imperative","boundary-in-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-data-502-nach-deploy","query":"seit dem deploy kommen nur noch 502er zurueck, schau mal was der container seitdem ausspuckt","language":"de","note":"Widened against the original author's single name: ops_triage's own catalog example is literally 'why is the API returning 502', so labelling this log_analyst-only would score the router against a preference rather than a fact. Both are right - log_analyst reads what the container prints, ops_triage diagnoses a 502 after a deploy - and the case still discriminates, because the user asked to LOOK, which rules out infrastructure_agent (mutates) and devops_coordinator (rollback).","expect":{"acceptable":["log_analyst","ops_triage"],"admitted":true},"tags":["data","imperative","boundary-in-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-data-slow-report-page","query":"one of our report pages takes forever since monday - can you check what the database is actually doing when that page opens?","language":"en","note":"Rewritten: the original said 'slow' and 'query', both lifted straight from sql_specialist's example 'optimize this slow query'. Same intent without the borrowed words - asking what the database does while one page loads is a plan/index question and only sql_specialist holds a live connection. log_analyst is the real near miss because forever means latency, but a log tells you WHICH request was slow, not which plan node caused it; kept strict on purpose, and a live route to log_analyst is a miss, not a bad label.","expect":{"acceptable":["sql_specialist"],"admitted":true},"tags":["data","bare-question","boundary-in-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-data-einwilligungsfeld","query":"wir muessen bei jedem nutzer mitspeichern ob er zugestimmt hat. das braucht das testsystem auch, und die bestehenden daten duerfen dabei nicht kaputtgehen","language":"de","note":"Rewritten because the original ('ein feld an den nutzern dran') read just as easily as a UI checkbox, which would have made the label undefendable. Storing a flag per user, on a second environment, without breaking the rows that are already there is an idempotent schema migration - sql_specialist. backend_coder is the temptation but is genuinely not right: it builds and SERVES a Node app, and nothing here asks for an endpoint or a running server. Zero shared tokens with sql_specialist.","expect":{"acceptable":["sql_specialist"],"admitted":true},"tags":["data","two-part","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-data-balken-pro-standort","query":"die auslastung pro standort die du gerade ausgerechnet hast, mach mir daraus bitte balken","language":"de","note":"Rewritten: the original ('umsaetze pro region ... balken') was chart_designer's own German catalog example 'Balkendiagramm der Umsaetze pro Region' with the words rearranged - invisible to the eval's token metric because umlauts drop out of its tokeniser, but written from the catalog all the same. Subject changed, intent kept: the numbers are stated to be computed already, so only rendering is left (chart_designer); data_analyst would redo work the query says is done, and diagram_designer is out because bars over sites are numbers, not structure.","expect":{"acceptable":["chart_designer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["data","follow-up","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-data-csv-von-url","query":"pulled the charging point list off https://opendata.koeln.de/ladesaeulen_2025.csv and its in your folder now - how many came online per year?","language":"en","note":"Rewritten twice over: the old URL contributed 'data' and 'dataset' as free token overlap with the target, and it left the file sitting on the web, which data_analyst cannot reach - it has read_file/spreadsheet_read but no fetcher, so the old label was wrong at the capability level. Now the file is stated to be local and the URL is provenance. A count grouped by year over one CSV is data_analyst; researcher stays the temptation because the line opens with a URL, but nobody is asked to find or cross-check sources.","expect":{"acceptable":["data_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["data","url","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-data-login-hammer","query":"someone keeps hammering our login page, can you tell from the logs how often and from where?","language":"en","note":"Counting authentication-failure bursts and the source addresses behind them is log_analyst's security-signal reading; recon_agent is the temptation because the request smells like an attack, but the user wants existing evidence read, not the perimeter probed, and asks for no scan or remediation. 'logs' is shared with the target and stays - naming the input is exactly how a user phrases this, and it is what separates the four agents in this cluster.","expect":{"acceptable":["log_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["data","bare-question","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-data-fehler-pro-stunde","query":"kannst du aus den logfiles von gestern rausziehen wie viele anfragen pro stunde schiefgegangen sind, und mir das als kurve zeigen?","language":"de","note":"Rewritten from the set's leakiest case ('error rate ... as a chart ... from the logs' shared error/rate/logs with log_analyst and chart with chart_designer - five distinctive words across two targets). Same boundary, now in native German with zero shared tokens: the per-hour counts have to be pulled out of raw log text first (log_analyst) but the stated deliverable is the curve (chart_designer), so either is a defensible first hop; data_analyst is excluded because the source is log text, not a tabular file, which its own catalog entry disclaims.","expect":{"acceptable":["log_analyst","chart_designer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["data","two-part","boundary-in-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-review-since-friday","query":"seit freitag sind da ein paar commits reingegangen, guck dir an was davon gefaehrlich werden koennte","language":"de","note":"The scope is a commit range, and that is the only thing separating diff_reviewer from code_analyst, which reads the checked-out tree and would happily report risks in code nobody touched; 'davon' pins the judgement to the new commits. quality_supervisor is not listed because nothing here is a finished deliverable measured against a brief.","expect":{"acceptable":["diff_reviewer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["review","imperative"]}
{"id":"live-review-pr-link","query":"here's the PR https://github.com/acme/widget/pull/214 - i want to land this today, is there anything in there that should worry me?","language":"en","note":"A pasted PR URL plus a ship-or-not verdict is diff_reviewer's merge-readiness job; git_developer also reads PRs but exists to OPERATE on them (open, comment, dispatch CI) and nothing here asks for a repo mutation. Reworded away from the original's 'is it safe to land', which echoed the catalog's own 'is this diff safe to merge'.","expect":{"acceptable":["diff_reviewer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["review","url"]}
{"id":"live-review-needs-a-test","query":"fehlt bei dem was ich geaendert hab noch irgendein test, oder passt das so?","language":"de","note":"Genuine in-cluster overlap: diff_reviewer answers it by spotting a behaviour change with no test in the change set, qa_guard by running the suite and seeing what the change is actually covered by, and the query says nothing about which evidence the user wants. coder and code_analyst are not listed because the ask is a verdict on coverage, not a test written or the tree read.","expect":{"acceptable":["diff_reviewer","qa_guard"],"admitted":true},"tags":["review","bare-question","follow-up"]}
{"id":"live-review-nobody-checked","query":"nobody has actually checked that yesterday's changes work - can you go through and tell me what breaks?","language":"en","note":"Something has to be executed before anyone can answer and the deliverable is a list of failures, which is qa_guard. Reworded away from the original's 'kick it all off ... what comes back red', which reads as dispatching a CI pipeline and made devops_coordinator and git_developer (ci check-run inspection) defensible answers; there is no deployment and no pipeline result to read here, and shell_agent is out because no command is named.","expect":{"acceptable":["qa_guard"],"admitted":true},"tags":["review","imperative"]}
{"id":"live-review-stacktrace-repro","query":"hier der stacktrace von heute frueh, stell das mal nach und guck ob der fix von gestern das ueberhaupt wegmacht","language":"de","note":"Reproducing a reported failure and then confirming yesterday's fix removes it is qa_guard's loop end to end; log_analyst is the trap because the input is a stack trace, but the user is not asking what the trace says, they are asking someone to make the bug happen again and prove it is gone.","expect":{"acceptable":["qa_guard"],"admitted":true},"tags":["review","pasted","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-review-goes-to-customer","query":"das geht morgen zum kunden raus, schau bitte ob was fehlt und ob da sachen drinstehen die wir so nicht rausgeben duerfen","language":"de","note":"Two-part by construction, one half pointing at each agent: 'ob was fehlt' is a completeness gate (quality_supervisor), 'was wir nicht rausgeben duerfen' is data-sensitivity and egress screening (policy_compliance_reviewer), and no agent in this catalog owns both. mail_agent is the cross-cluster trap, since 'geht zum kunden raus' reads as sending, but nothing is being sent.","expect":{"acceptable":["quality_supervisor","policy_compliance_reviewer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["review","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-review-segen-von-oben","query":"koennen wir die kundenliste einfach an den externen anbieter geben oder braucht das vorher einen segen von oben?","language":"de","note":"A pure allowed-or-not question with an approval half, which is policy_compliance_reviewer's whole remit. quality_supervisor is the in-cluster near miss but it judges whether a deliverable is complete and grounded, never whether an action is permitted; mail_agent and api_integrator would try to perform the handover instead of screening it.","expect":{"acceptable":["policy_compliance_reviewer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["review","bare-question"]}
{"id":"live-review-rollout-signoff","query":"attached is friday's rollout plan, it drops the old tables - what in there needs a sign-off before anyone runs it?","language":"en","note":"The user wants the approval-gated and destructive steps in a plan named back to them, which is policy_compliance_reviewer; devops_coordinator is the trap because of the rollout framing but it would execute the promotion rather than screen it, and sql_specialist would look at the DROP statements rather than at who has to say yes. Highest residual catalog overlap in the set (shared token 'plan'), kept because 'sign-off' is a real paraphrase of the catalog's 'approval'.","expect":{"acceptable":["policy_compliance_reviewer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["review","pasted","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-review-good-enough-to-forward","query":"is that write-up actually good enough to forward, or did it skip half of what i asked for?","language":"en","note":"Judging a finished draft against the original ask and returning ship-or-rerun is quality_supervisor; source_verifier is the trap since it also audits an existing draft, but it checks claim-to-source support and nothing here is about sources, and qa_guard is not listed because there is nothing to execute.","expect":{"acceptable":["quality_supervisor"],"admitted":true},"tags":["review","bare-question","follow-up"]}
{"id":"live-infra-container-schleife","query":"hab das hier vom server kopiert: container startet, laeuft 20 sekunden, exit code 137, dann wieder von vorn. was ist da los?","language":"de","note":"A pasted crash symptom plus 'was ist da los' asks for a cause, and separating an OOM kill from a bad config is exactly ops_triage's read-only diagnosis; shell_agent is the tempting miss because the paste looks like terminal output inviting another command, but the user wants the reason rather than more stdout, and infrastructure_agent only becomes right once somebody has decided what to change.","expect":{"acceptable":["ops_triage"],"admitted":true},"tags":["infra","paste","question"]}
{"id":"live-infra-zertifikat-ausrollen","query":"zieh das neue zertifikat auf die drei webserver und starte die danach der reihe nach durch","language":"de","note":"Pushing a file onto three remote hosts and then recycling them in order is a mutating multi-host change and only infrastructure_agent performs it; shell_agent is the tempting miss because each individual step is an ssh command, but it runs ONE requested command and reports raw output instead of sequencing three machines, and devops_coordinator is out because nothing is being released or promoted.","expect":{"acceptable":["infrastructure_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["infra","imperative","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-infra-wartungsfenster-alarme","query":"samstag zwischen 8 und 10 machen wir wartung an der datenbank, stell die alarme solange ab und danach wieder an","language":"de","note":"Silencing and un-silencing alerting for a bounded window is a change to the monitoring backend, which only infrastructure_agent can make; notification_agent is the tempting miss because the sentence is about 'alarme', but it merely SENDS messages to chat channels, and ops_triage can list existing silences without being able to create one.","expect":{"acceptable":["infrastructure_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["infra","imperative","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-infra-gestern-live-zurueck","query":"das was gestern abend live gegangen ist macht mehr kaputt als es hilft, nimm es wieder runter und lass den stand von vorgestern laufen","language":"de","note":"Picking the smallest safe scope back to the last good release is devops_coordinator's rollback decision while the rollback itself is a release mutation infrastructure_agent executes, so both are defensible entry points; git_developer is the tempting miss because 'nimm es wieder runter' reads as a revert, but what went live is an environment, not a commit.","expect":{"acceptable":["devops_coordinator","infrastructure_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["infra","imperative","two-part","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-infra-rollout-haengt","query":"der rollout von heute mittag haengt seit ner halben stunde bei der haelfte der maschinen. guck mal woran das klemmt, und wenn sich da nix mehr tut, zurueck auf die vorige version","language":"de","note":"The first half is read-only diagnosis of a stuck rollout (ops_triage) and the second half is a conditional rollback decision (devops_coordinator), and whichever is entered first hands the other half over, so both count; infrastructure_agent stays out because nothing is to be changed at all unless the rollback condition actually fires.","expect":{"acceptable":["ops_triage","devops_coordinator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["infra","two-part","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-infra-endlich-durch-dann-prod","query":"tests on main are finally all passing. can you get that onto prod - two boxes first though, and leave it an hour before the rest follows","language":"en","note":"A staged rollout with a soak window before the remainder is devops_coordinator's canary decision, but the partial rollout and its later completion are infrastructure_agent's actual work, so both belong; the anaphor 'that' has its referent in the first sentence, and the wording deliberately avoids 'ci', 'green' and 'build', which are devops_coordinator's own catalog words.","expect":{"acceptable":["devops_coordinator","infrastructure_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["infra","followup","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-infra-staging-token-401","query":"here's the staging one https://staging.acme.io/v1/orders - do you get anything back on that with the token you have, or is the 401 my fault?","language":"en","note":"Issuing one authenticated request and reporting what comes back, including whether the auth header or the service is at fault, is api_integrator's whole job; browser_agent is the tempting miss because a URL is handed over, but there is no page to open, no form and no screenshot, and the URL is an unrelated staging API rather than the LM-Studio example api_integrator's own description carries.","expect":{"acceptable":["api_integrator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["infra","url"]}
{"id":"live-infra-partner-schickt-nichts","query":"der partner sagt er schickt uns die bestellungen, bei uns kommt aber nichts an. kannst du pruefen ob die adresse von aussen ueberhaupt antwortet?","language":"de","note":"The concrete instruction - does that address answer from outside - is api_integrator's reachability check, but the framing 'nothing arrives on our side' is live-failure triage and ops_triage probes endpoints too, and which of the two is right only becomes clear once the probe says whether the fault is the URL or our own service.","expect":{"acceptable":["api_integrator","ops_triage"],"admitted":true},"tags":["infra","question","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-infra-felder-kommen-nicht","query":"here's the field list from their api docs - try it against the real thing and tell me which of those actually come back and which are always empty","language":"en","note":"Comparing a documented field list against what the live endpoint really returns cannot be answered without issuing the request, which is api_integrator's; code_analyst is the tempting miss because a pasted list looks like something to read statically, and backend_coder is wrong because nothing is being built or served here.","expect":{"acceptable":["api_integrator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["infra","paste"]}
{"id":"live-swarmmeta-kommt-nie-zum-ende","query":"der researcher macht bei groesseren sachen ewig weiter und kommt nie zu einem ende, kannst du da was an seiner anweisung aendern","language":"de","note":"In-cluster boundary: an agent that runs on and never concludes is exactly prompt_optimizer's stopping-behaviour diagnosis, but 'aendere was an seiner anweisung' asks for the edit to actually land, which is swarm_maintainer's durable prompt edit - the query does not disambiguate and both are defensible. code_analyst is not defensible: nothing here is source code, only how an agent is instructed. REWRITTEN from the original: it said 'dreht sich im kreis ... was drehen' (clumsy German, and a near-restatement of prompt_optimizer's own example query 'the coder agent keeps looping - what prompt change fixes it').","expect":{"acceptable":["prompt_optimizer","swarm_maintainer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["swarmmeta","imperative","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-swarmmeta-zuschlaege-von-hand","query":"wir tippen jeden monat dieselben zuschlaege von hand in die tabelle, das muesste das system doch selber ausrechnen koennen","language":"de","note":"In-cluster boundary: a repeatable calculation over a table with no network is tool_developer's pure-compute remit, while 'das system muesste das koennen' is a request for the swarm to gain a capability, which is swarm_maintainer's. data_analyst is the tempting cross-cluster answer and is deliberately excluded - it would compute this month's number once, and the stated complaint is that it recurs every month by hand. Kept verbatim: zero lexical overlap with either target, and it reads as something a German speaker types.","expect":{"acceptable":["tool_developer","swarm_maintainer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["swarmmeta","statement","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-swarmmeta-architektenmail-ablegen","query":"die mail vom architekten von heute gehoert zum dachausbau, pack sie zu dem was wir sonst zu dem bau gesammelt haben","language":"de","note":"Filing an existing message against a long-running building project is process_memory_keeper's core move. mail_agent is the tempting cross-cluster answer because the object is an email - and the original phrasing ('leg sie da mit dazu') read just as naturally as moving it into a mail FOLDER, which mail_agent genuinely owns, so the single-name expectation was not defensible as written. The destination is now a cross-source collection about the build, not a mailbox. document_intake is out: nothing is being extracted from the file.","expect":{"acceptable":["process_memory_keeper"],"admitted":true},"tags":["swarmmeta","imperative","crosscluster"]}
{"id":"live-swarmmeta-falsche-felder","query":"der coder ruft unser pdf-werkzeug jedes mal mit den falschen feldern auf und probiert es dann fuenfmal, liegt das an ihm oder an dem werkzeug","language":"de","note":"In-cluster boundary, and the query states the tension itself: a caller that mis-invokes and then retries is tool-use convergence, which is prompt_optimizer's subject, but a signature nobody can call correctly is the tool's own problem, which is tool_developer's. swarm_maintainer is not listed because nothing is being created or wired yet - the user is still asking which of the two it is. Query kept; the shape tag was corrected from 'twopart' to 'question' - it is one either/or question, not two requests.","expect":{"acceptable":["prompt_optimizer","tool_developer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["swarmmeta","question","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-swarmmeta-vorgangsnummer-url","query":"der vorgang bei der hausverwaltung laeuft jetzt unter https://hv-mueller-gmbh.de/vorgaenge/4711, schreib das bitte zum streit ums treppenhaus dazu","language":"de","note":"A reference is being recorded against a named ongoing dispute, which is process_memory_keeper; the referent (the treppenhaus dispute) is named in the query. browser_agent is the tempting cross-cluster answer because of the link, but nothing is asked to be opened or fetched. REWRITTEN only in the host: the original used portal.example.de, which handed browser_agent the tokens 'portal' and 'example' straight out of its own 'log into the portal' example - a lexical gift to the wrong agent (overlap 0.0441 -> 0.0141).","expect":{"acceptable":["process_memory_keeper"],"admitted":true},"tags":["swarmmeta","url","crosscluster"]}
{"id":"live-swarmmeta-overclaiming-summarizer","query":"the summarizer keeps saying it read things it never opened. what would you tell it differently so it stops doing that?","language":"en","note":"An agent that makes claims it cannot support, plus a request for what to say to it instead, is prompt_optimizer's grounding remit. The hypothetical ('what WOULD you tell it') is what keeps it advisory, which is why swarm_maintainer is deliberately not listed - the request stops before the edit. quality_supervisor and qa_guard are the tempting cross-cluster answers because unsupported claims are what they police, but no output is being checked here. REWRITTEN: the original used 'what would you change in its wording', which is prompt_optimizer's own catalog vocabulary and gave this case the highest overlap in the set (0.0649 -> 0.0375).","expect":{"acceptable":["prompt_optimizer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["swarmmeta","question","crosscluster"]}
{"id":"live-swarmmeta-pasted-instructions","query":"pasted the instructions for our support intake agent below - it still offers to open a ticket every time even though that text says it must not. can you fix that?","language":"en","note":"In-cluster boundary: a pasted instruction block whose behaviour contradicts what the block says is prompt_optimizer's smallest-change review, while 'can you fix that' asks for the edit to land, which is swarm_maintainer. REWRITTEN: the original complaint was 'it never stops asking follow-up questions', i.e. the same stopping-behaviour diagnosis as live-swarmmeta-kommt-nie-zum-ende with the same acceptable pair - two cases that pass or fail together measure one thing, not two. document_intake is the tempting cross-cluster answer on the word 'intake', but the subject is an agent's instructions, not a file to extract from.","expect":{"acceptable":["prompt_optimizer","swarm_maintainer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["swarmmeta","pasted","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-swarmmeta-make-it-permanent","query":"that check you ran over our open tickets last week worked - can we make it happen by itself every monday, i shouldn't have to ask each time","language":"en","note":"A follow-up that assumes earlier context but names its referent: turning a one-off run into a standing, self-starting routine is job creation, which is swarm_maintainer. calendar_agent is the tempting cross-cluster answer because 'every monday' reads as a recurring appointment - but an appointment does not run anything; devops_coordinator schedules deployments, not swarm routines. REWRITTEN: the original was 'that monthly report thing ... runs on its own every month', which is swarm_maintainer's own example 'create a new scene for weekly reports' with the interval changed.","expect":{"acceptable":["swarm_maintainer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["swarmmeta","followup","crosscluster"]}
{"id":"live-swarmmeta-price-list-parser","query":"our supplier sends the price list as a plain text dump with everything lined up in columns and someone reformats it by hand every week - can you look at one and build us something that turns it into a proper table?","language":"en","note":"Two asks in one sentence, both pure compute over a local plaintext file with no egress, which is tool_developer's remit. coder is the closest miss and is deliberately excluded: it runs a script to return one computed result, while the stated complaint is that this recurs every week - the user wants the capability to exist. document_intake is out by its own stated boundary (BINARY or non-plaintext attachments) and data_analyst computes over the numbers rather than producing the converter. REWRITTEN: the original was an .ics recurrence parser, which is a near-verbatim restatement of tool_developer's own example query 'implement a tool that parses iCal files' - and its note argued against calendar_agent while missing document_intake, which lists .ics in its tags.","expect":{"acceptable":["tool_developer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["swarmmeta","twopart","crosscluster"]}
{"id":"live-media-qr-anmeldung","query":"kannst du nen qr code machen der auf die anmeldeseite zeigt? den kleben wir auf den flyer","language":"de","note":"image_creator is the only agent that can emit a QR code at all, so this is the cluster's one genuinely single-answer case; image_sourcer finds existing photos on the web and could never make one. The flyer is the cross-cluster bait - content_writer and web_coder own printed and web layout - but what is asked for is the code itself, not the page it points at. Rewritten off the guest-wifi payload, because 'generate a QR code for the WiFi credentials' is a verbatim example query inside image_creator's own catalog entry and a near-translation of it would have passed under a substring router.","expect":{"acceptable":["image_creator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["media","imperative"]}
{"id":"live-media-rechtlich-sauber","query":"fuer die broschuere brauchen wir noch aufnahmen vom alten wasserturm, aber nur welche die wir auch wirklich verwenden duerfen","language":"de","note":"Pictures of one real, named building plus a usage-rights constraint is sourcing and verification end to end; generation cannot satisfy 'photos of that tower', so image_creator is out. researcher is the tempting miss from another cluster - it also searches the web and the sentence reads like a brief - but it gathers facts and prose, never image files with a licence. Rewritten from 'die vier gebaeuden', which was both anaphoric with no referent and a direct echo of image_sourcer's own example query 'get working image URLs for these four buildings'; 'aufnahmen' and 'verwenden duerfen' are user words, where 'lizenzfrei' would have been a literal tag.","expect":{"acceptable":["image_sourcer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["media","need","cross-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-media-screenshot-tickets","query":"auf dem screenshot von der statusseite den du vorhin gemacht hast, was steht da bei den offenen tickets?","language":"de","note":"The capture already exists inside the run and the user wants a value read out of it, which is interpretation rather than navigation - the nastiest lexical trap in the cluster, because browser_agent owns the token 'screenshot' and shares it with the target at the same weight. Rewritten to say the capture came from the run: the original read as a user-pasted image, which makes document_intake genuinely defensible (it extracts exact text from uploaded images), and a case with two defensible answers and one listed is a broken case, not a hard one.","expect":{"acceptable":["vision_browser_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["media","question","followup","cross-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-media-foto-und-titelbild","query":"such mir ein gutes foto von der neuen messehalle, und fuers titelbild brauch ich noch was gezeichnetes im gleichen stil","language":"de","note":"Two requests in one sentence that fall on opposite sides of the cluster's main line: a usable photo of a real building is image_sourcer, something drawn for the title image is image_creator. Either can legitimately lead and hand the other the style reference, so both are listed; what the case measures is that a two-part media brief does not fall out of the cluster into content_writer, which owns the brochure the two assets are for. Rewritten away from 'frauenkirche' and 'cover', both of which appear verbatim in the cluster's catalog entries ('Bild-URLs der Frauenkirche', 'watercolor cover illustration'); 'titelbild' is also the more native German word here.","expect":{"acceptable":["image_sourcer","image_creator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["media","two-part","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-media-schaubild-kuerzen","query":"das schaubild von vorhin is zu voll, mach eine version nur mit den drei hauptschritten","language":"de","note":"A follow-up whose referent is named inside the sentence - the schaubild, and what it contains are steps - so the only open question is which media agent redraws a process. image_creator is the in-cluster pull because 'schaubild' covers artwork as well as structure, and chart_designer is the cross-cluster one, but steps are structure and not numbers, and a flowchart is the form that can actually be trimmed to three of them. Kept unchanged: it shares no token at all with diagram_designer's catalog text.","expect":{"acceptable":["diagram_designer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["media","followup"]}
{"id":"live-media-call-order","query":"can you draw up which service calls which when a new signup comes in? needs to go into the handover doc","language":"en","note":"The order in which named components call each other is exactly what diagram_designer renders as a sequence, and it only diagrams structure already supplied - which this query supplies. chart_designer is the tempting miss from another cluster ('draw' plus a doc deliverable), but there is not a single number to plot; image_creator would return artwork instead of a readable structure. Rewritten from 'how the three backends and the queue talk to each other', which was the same case as the corpus's existing live-architecture-picture in the other language; asking for call ORDER rather than static connectivity makes it measure something that case does not, and 'signup' replaces an order/Bestellung payload that diagram_designer lists as its own example.","expect":{"acceptable":["diagram_designer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["media","imperative","cross-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-media-url-still-loads","query":"someone sent me this one for the deck, https://cdn.city-archive.org/media/harbour-crane-1200.jpg - does it still open for you, and is that really the old crane on it?","language":"en","note":"Fetching an image URL, confirming it is reachable and confirming it shows the right subject is image_sourcer's job end to end. vision_browser_analyst is the real in-cluster pull, because subject confirmation is its trade and image_sourcer even advertises 'visual subject confirmation' - but it was cut from acceptable rather than listed: it has no fetch or navigate tool, only capture, so it cannot act on a bare URL at all, and listing an agent that would fail the request is how a recall metric stops meaning anything. researcher can fetch a URL but does not handle images. Deliberately not a Wikimedia link: 'wikimedia' and 'commons' are literal tags on image_sourcer.","expect":{"acceptable":["image_sourcer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["media","url"]}
{"id":"live-media-filter-icon","query":"we need a small icon for the settings screen, flat, single colour, should read as a filter","language":"en","note":"An icon authored to a style spec is vector creation, and image_creator is the only agent that hand-writes SVG. image_sourcer is the in-cluster pull - one could go looking for a free icon set - but the brief describes something that does not exist yet, and sourcing is scoped to licensed images of real subjects; web_coder owns the settings screen but not the asset on it. Kept unchanged: zero shared tokens with image_creator's catalog text, because the query never says svg, vector or logo.","expect":{"acceptable":["image_creator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["media","imperative","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-research-url-crosscheck","query":"grab the throughput numbers off https://example.com/blog/bench-2026 and see if anyone else has measured the same thing or if they're the only ones saying it","language":"en","note":"Fetching a page that is not on hand yet and then hunting for a second, unrelated measurement is fresh external lookup, which is researcher; browser_agent is the tempting wrong answer because the query carries a URL, but there is nothing to click, log into or fill in, and evidence_analyst is wrong because the second source does not exist yet so there is nothing to reconcile.","expect":{"acceptable":["researcher"],"admitted":true},"tags":["research","url","two-part","cross-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-research-ssh-advisory","query":"weiss man schon was genaueres zu der neuen ssh luecke und gibts dafuer schon einen patch?","language":"de","note":"Reading what has been published about a vulnerability and whether a fix shipped is ordinary source lookup and the catalog assigns advisory reading to researcher explicitly; recon_agent and network_auditor_agent are the tempting wrong answers from the pentest swarm because the words smell like security, but nothing here touches a live system.","expect":{"acceptable":["researcher"],"admitted":true},"tags":["research","bare-question","cross-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-research-thread-short-version","query":"i pasted the whole mail back and forth below - just tell me what it boils down to, dont read anything into it","language":"en","note":"A flat faithful restatement of one body of already-readable text is summarizer; meeting_briefing_agent is the tempting wrong answer because it also works from mail, but the user wants the short version, not owners, blockers and next actions, and explicitly forbids reading anything into it.","expect":{"acceptable":["summarizer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["research","pasted","imperative","cross-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-research-forty-pages","query":"die seite ist ewig lang und ich muss gleich weg. schreib mir in fuenf punkten was drinsteht, aber alles wo geld drin vorkommt muss bleiben","language":"de","note":"Condensing one long readable page into key points while keeping the figures intact is summarizer; evidence_analyst is wrong because there is a single source and nothing to reconcile, and researcher is wrong because nothing is to be looked up.","expect":{"acceptable":["summarizer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["research","imperative"]}
{"id":"live-research-footnotes-dont-hold","query":"der entwurf unten ist von einem kollegen, in den fussnoten steht zeug das ich nirgends wiederfinde. geh das durch und sag mir was davon haltbar ist","language":"de","note":"An existing draft audited claim by claim against references that cannot be found is source_verifier's fabricated-reference work; quality_supervisor is the tempting wrong answer because it also reviews drafts, but it judges completeness against the brief and never chases a single reference to see whether it exists.","expect":{"acceptable":["source_verifier"],"admitted":true},"tags":["research","pasted","imperative","cross-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-research-three-reports-disagree","query":"wir haben zu dem quartal von drei stellen zahlen und keine passt zur anderen. bau mir daraus eine uebersicht wo ich sehe was gesichert ist und was nur jemand behauptet","language":"de","note":"Three prose sources that contradict each other need reconciliation with attribution and a confirmed-versus-tentative split, which is evidence_analyst; data_analyst is the tempting wrong answer because the conflict is about numbers, but the numbers sit inside reports, not in a table to compute over.","expect":{"acceptable":["evidence_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["research","imperative","cross-cluster"]}
{"id":"live-research-ground-what-we-have","query":"we have the notes from both calls and the two product pages we already saved. sort out what we can actually stand behind and where each bit came from","language":"en","note":"The material is already collected and the ask is to separate what holds up while keeping each item's origin, which is evidence_analyst; researcher is wrong because the query says the sources are saved already and asks for nothing new to be found.","expect":{"acceptable":["evidence_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["research","imperative"]}
{"id":"live-research-half-done-notes","query":"ich hab schon ein paar notizen und zwei seiten offen, aber irgendwas fehlt noch. such den rest und pack das dann mit dem zusammen was ich schon hab","language":"de","note":"Boundary inside the cluster: 'such den rest' is fresh external lookup and belongs to researcher, 'pack das mit dem zusammen was ich schon hab' is merging it with material already on hand and belongs to evidence_analyst; both are defensible and which should lead depends on how much is still missing, which the user cannot say either.","expect":{"acceptable":["researcher","evidence_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["research","two-part","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-research-is-that-true","query":"the text they sent says the eu banned this kind of cookie tracking in 2024. is that actually true?","language":"en","note":"Boundary inside the cluster: judging one statement inside a text the user already holds is source_verifier, while establishing the underlying fact from outside sources is researcher; both are defensible because the user wants the sentence judged and the fact settled in the same breath, and the statement is concrete enough that either agent knows what to check.","expect":{"acceptable":["source_verifier","researcher"],"admitted":true},"tags":["research","bare-question","pasted","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-research-dead-link-followup","query":"von den links die du mir zu dem foerderprogramm rausgesucht hast geht einer ins leere. pruef die nochmal durch","language":"de","note":"Boundary inside the cluster: a dead reference is source_verifier's broken-url work, but re-finding the page behind it is researcher's lookup; the follow-up shape is safe because the referent ('die links zu dem foerderprogramm') is named inside the query rather than left to a prior turn.","expect":{"acceptable":["source_verifier","researcher"],"admitted":true},"tags":["research","follow-up","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-coordinate-rollback-yesterday","query":"der neue stand macht nur aerger, schieb bitte wieder den von gestern drauf","language":"de","note":"Putting yesterday's build back in front of users is a revert DECISION about which version runs where, and devops_coordinator is the one of the four that owns it and hands the machine work down. infrastructure_agent is the strongest wrong answer because it is what would physically perform the rollback (helm rollback, redeploy), but its own entry places it downstream of devops_coordinator; git_developer is tempting for the same reason and its entry explicitly routes a ship-to-environment request here.","expect":{"acceptable":["devops_coordinator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["coordinate","imperative","cross-cluster-trap"]}
{"id":"live-coordinate-markets-overnight","query":"did much happen on the markets while i was asleep?","language":"en","note":"One current value with nothing to compare and nothing to assemble is the freshness-only scope web_task_coordinator exists for: one live retrieval, relayed. researcher is the tempting wrong answer because 'markets' smells like a topic to investigate, but researcher's OWN entry sends single freshness lookups (news, scores, weather, quotes) here, so the catalog gives a clean tiebreak rather than a matter of taste.","expect":{"acceptable":["web_task_coordinator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["coordinate","bare-question","cross-cluster-trap"]}
{"id":"live-coordinate-relaunch-approach","query":"wir wollen im herbst den kompletten kundenbereich neu bauen, wie gehen wir das am besten an?","language":"de","note":"Boundary inside the cluster: 'wie gehen wir das an' asks for the approach, which is project_planner's phased breakdown with an ordering and a rough schedule - but rebuilding a whole customer area is also the multi-area shape mission_coordinator is selected on, and plenty of users phrasing it this way want the work started, not a document. Both readings are honest, so both are listed; what would be wrong is a builder like web_coder starting on a page before anyone agreed on scope.","expect":{"acceptable":["project_planner","mission_coordinator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["coordinate","bare-question","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-coordinate-vendor-decision-memo","query":"finde raus welche vier anbieter ueberhaupt in frage kommen, schau dir preise support und datenschutz an und mach mir daraus eine entscheidungsvorlage","language":"de","note":"Three separate dimensions to gather plus a drafted document at the end is the decompose-then-merge shape mission_coordinator is selected on: it splits the lookups across specialists and hands the writing to an author agent. researcher is the tempting wrong answer because the first verb is a lookup, but researcher covers one topic and never produces the merged recommendation; content_writer is tempting because of the memo at the end, but it would write from a brief nobody has gathered yet; project_planner is the near miss inside the cluster and is wrong because the user wants the finished comparison, not a plan for producing it.","expect":{"acceptable":["mission_coordinator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["coordinate","two-part","cross-cluster-trap"]}
{"id":"live-coordinate-run-url-to-prod","query":"https://github.com/acme/billing/actions/runs/18392 finally passed - can you get that build out to customers tonight?","language":"en","note":"A pasted CI run link plus 'get it out tonight' is an environment promotion with a green-check gate in front of it, which is devops_coordinator's scope end to end. git_developer is the tempting wrong answer since the URL is a GitHub Actions run and git_developer does read check runs and dispatch workflows - but its catalog entry explicitly routes a ship-to-users request here, and what is being asked for is a decision about environments, not about the repository.","expect":{"acceptable":["devops_coordinator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["coordinate","url","two-part","cross-cluster-trap"]}
{"id":"live-coordinate-order-the-workstreams","query":"take the five workstreams we listed and put them in an order where nobody is waiting on someone else, with a rough week for each","language":"en","note":"The ask is the sequence and the dates, not the work: ordering so nothing blocks and putting a week against each item is what project_planner produces and then hands on. mission_coordinator is the near miss inside the cluster and is wrong here because it would begin executing the five workstreams, which nothing in the sentence asks for. It is a follow-up turn, but the referent ('the five workstreams') is named in the query, and routing needs the shape rather than the contents.","expect":{"acceptable":["project_planner"],"admitted":true},"tags":["coordinate","follow-up","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-coordinate-pasted-to-phases","query":"ich hab dir die offenen punkte reinkopiert, mach da bitte einen fahrplan in etappen draus und schreib dazu was am ende von jeder etappe fertig sein muss","language":"de","note":"Rewritten from a version framed as pasted MEETING NOTES, which made meeting_briefing_agent at least as defensible as the target and turned a single-name expectation into the labeller's taste. Stripped of that framing the ask is unambiguous: stages plus what must be done at the end of each is a phased plan with acceptance criteria, and project_planner is the only one of the four that writes the artifact instead of delegating. summarizer is the remaining trap because something was pasted, but the user wants work turned into a schedule, not text condensed; mission_coordinator is wrong because nothing is to be executed yet.","expect":{"acceptable":["project_planner"],"admitted":true},"tags":["coordinate","pasted","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-coordinate-db-cutover-weekend","query":"am wochenende stellen wir auf die neue datenbank um, sorg dafuer dass vorher jemand drueberschaut und hinterher wirklich getestet wird","language":"de","note":"Boundary inside the cluster: a weekend switchover with a review before and a test after is devops_coordinator's exact gate-rollout-verify pattern, but this is a data migration rather than a CI/CD release - which is where devops' own entry draws its scope - and it pulls several specialists in sequence, the multi-area shape mission_coordinator is selected on. Either winner is defensible; a real miss is infrastructure_agent, which would perform the move without the two gates the user explicitly asked for.","expect":{"acceptable":["devops_coordinator","mission_coordinator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["coordinate","two-part","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-coordinate-pitch-thursday","query":"we pitch on thursday and i still need last quarters numbers, what the competition shipped since then, and a story that ties it together - can you get that done?","language":"en","note":"Three distinct sub-topics - our own figures, the outside market, and a narrative binding them - collapsed into one deliverable with a deadline is the multi-area shape mission_coordinator is selected on; it runs the slices in parallel and routes the drafting to an author. data_analyst, researcher and content_writer are each a tempting wrong answer because each owns exactly one of the three slices and would deliver a third of the request; project_planner is wrong because Thursday leaves no room for a plan about the work.","expect":{"acceptable":["mission_coordinator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["coordinate","imperative","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-coordinate-rain-saturday","query":"the outdoor half of the party is on saturday afternoon - is it going to rain on us?","language":"en","note":"A forecast for a named day is one live value with nothing to synthesise, and web_task_coordinator is the only one of the four scoped to that lookup; researcher's entry hands weather here explicitly. calendar_agent is the tempting wrong answer because a weekday and an event are both in the sentence, but nothing is being scheduled, moved or looked up in a calendar - the user already knows when the party is and is asking about the sky. Follow-up shape: it assumes an earlier turn about the party, but carries its own referent.","expect":{"acceptable":["web_task_coordinator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["coordinate","follow-up","cross-cluster-trap"]}
{"id":"live-coordinate-after-update-complaints","query":"seit dem update heute frueh melden die ersten kunden fehler, wie gehen wir vor?","language":"de","note":"'Wie gehen wir vor' straight after a release went out is the revert-or-fix-forward call devops_coordinator owns - but working out what actually broke before anyone decides is ops_triage's read-only diagnosis and an equally fair reading of the same sentence, so both are listed rather than my preferring one. The wrong answer is infrastructure_agent, which would start changing the running system before anyone has decided what should change. Kept deliberately non-discriminating between the two: splitting it into a cause-known and a cause-unknown variant would give devops_coordinator a third single-name case.","expect":{"acceptable":["devops_coordinator","ops_triage"],"admitted":true},"tags":["coordinate","bare-question","incident"]}
{"id":"live-authoring-folien-aus-jahresrueckblick","query":"der text zum jahresrueckblick steht jetzt - mach mir daraus noch acht folien fuer die runde am montag","language":"de","note":"content_writer is the only entry in the whole 49-agent catalog that builds slide decks, so paper_author - the in-cluster near miss - is wrong because it produces documents and never a deck, and the referent of the follow-up ('der text zum jahresrueckblick') is named inside the query so the case stays resolvable on its own.","expect":{"acceptable":["content_writer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["authoring","follow-up","imperative"]}
{"id":"live-authoring-preisseite-umschreiben","query":"our pricing page reads like a tax form - https://acme.example/pricing. the current text is already in the folder, just redo the wording so a normal person gets it","language":"en","note":"The deliverable is new wording for copy the user says is already in the folder, which content_writer can read with its own file tools, so the live URL is a pure distractor - browser_agent would have been defensible only if the page still had to be fetched (content_writer holds no fetch tool at all), and web_coder is wrong because no markup or behaviour changes, only the words.","expect":{"acceptable":["content_writer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["authoring","url","pasted"]}
{"id":"live-authoring-kunden-umstellung-belegbar","query":"hab oben die stichpunkte vom chef reinkopiert. daraus soll ein text fuer die kunden werden, gut lesbar, aber die zahlen muss ich hinterher auch belegen koennen","language":"de","note":"Boundary inside the cluster: 'gut lesbar' for customers is content_writer's audience-facing prose while 'die zahlen muss ich belegen koennen' is exactly paper_author's source-grounded mode with a traceable reference trail, and because the query names neither a marketing channel nor a citation style both are defensible - this is the pair the catalog separates on a facet a real user never states.","expect":{"acceptable":["content_writer","paper_author"],"admitted":true},"tags":["authoring","boundary","pasted","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-authoring-dokument-aus-notizen","query":"aus den notizen und links die wir schon gesammelt haben soll jetzt ein ordentliches dokument werden, und unten drunter gehoert hin wo das alles herkommt","language":"de","note":"The sources are stated as already collected and the user asks for an attribution section underneath, which is paper_author's evidence-ledger-plus-references shape; researcher is the tempting miss from the research cluster because 'links/quellen' sounds like source hunting, but the hunt is over and researcher explicitly does not compose the document.","expect":{"acceptable":["paper_author"],"admitted":true},"tags":["authoring","imperative","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-authoring-board-case","query":"the numbers and the offers from both vendors are in already. what i need now is the written case for dropping the old stack - the board will pick at every claim in it, so it has to hold up","language":"en","note":"The evidence is stated as already in, so paper_author's own refuse-on-a-thin-ledger rule does not fire and what is left is one sustained argument that will be attacked on its substance; meeting_briefing_agent is the trap because 'board' suggests a status packet with owners and next actions, and content_writer is wrong because this is neither marketing nor editorial prose.","expect":{"acceptable":["paper_author"],"admitted":true},"tags":["authoring","imperative","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-authoring-sicherheitscheck-dokument","query":"kannst du aus dem was wir bei dem sicherheitscheck gefunden haben ein dokument machen? vorne soll die chefin lesen koennen wie schlimm es ist, hinten braucht die technik details","language":"de","note":"Boundary inside the cluster: findings from a security check plus a non-technical-then-technical split is report_writer_agent's exact deliverable, but the query never names an engagement, a scope or severity ratings, so a general source-grounded write-up by paper_author is defensible too - pentest_coordinator is the wrong answer because it would open another phase instead of producing the document.","expect":{"acceptable":["report_writer_agent","paper_author"],"admitted":true},"tags":["authoring","boundary","question","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-authoring-engagement-abschluss","query":"we're done poking at their boxes. pull everything we turned up into one writeup, worst stuff first, and say what they have to fix","language":"en","note":"The end of an offensive engagement in a user's own words: aggregating and de-duplicating findings in severity order with remediation is report_writer_agent's only job, while paper_author is the in-cluster near miss that neither dedupes nor rates findings, and pentest_coordinator would start another phase instead of producing the deliverable.","expect":{"acceptable":["report_writer_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["authoring","imperative","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-authoring-vertrag-ausstieg","query":"ich hab den vertrag hochgeladen - bis wann muss ich kuendigen, wenn ich naechstes jahr da rauswill?","language":"de","note":"A question about an uploaded binary contract that nothing can answer until document_intake has extracted it; summarizer is the tempting miss from the condensation cluster because this sounds like 'tell me what is in this', but summarizer only works on text that is already readable.","expect":{"acceptable":["document_intake"],"admitted":true},"tags":["authoring","question"]}
{"id":"live-authoring-aufnahme-als-text","query":"die aufnahme von dem termin gestern liegt im ordner, ich brauch das mal als text - will nicht nochmal ne stunde zuhoeren","language":"de","note":"A media file that must be transcribed before any other agent can touch it, and document_intake is the only entry that transcribes audio and video; meeting_briefing_agent is the tempting miss from the briefing cluster because 'termin' suggests meeting notes, but the user asks for what was said, not for a briefing with owners and next actions.","expect":{"acceptable":["document_intake"],"admitted":true},"tags":["authoring","imperative"]}
{"id":"live-authoring-lieferantendateien-zum-kunden","query":"there are three files from the supplier in the folder, two scans and an excel file. i need one readable thing out of that i can send back to the customer","language":"en","note":"Boundary inside the cluster: the blocking first step is turning scans and a sheet into readable content (document_intake) while the user names only the end product, customer-facing prose (content_writer), and routing straight to the writer - which would compose from files it cannot read - is a real failure mode, so both entry points count as correct here.","expect":{"acceptable":["document_intake","content_writer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["authoring","boundary","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-security-full-engagement","query":"der kunde hat uns schriftlich freigegeben, plan den kompletten angriffstest und halt die einzelnen phasen zusammen","language":"de","note":"A full authorized engagement: planning plus driving the phased work end to end, which only pentest_coordinator does (it sets scope and commands recon/audit/exploit/report). Uses colloquial 'angriffstest' and 'schriftlich freigegeben' rather than the catalog's Penetrationstest/autorisiert, so overlap is low. Tempting wrong answer is researcher (desk-based CVE/advisory reading); rejected because the user wants a coordinated live assessment against their own authorized target, not sources looked up.","expect":{"acceptable":["pentest_coordinator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","command"]}
{"id":"live-security-what-is-open","query":"kurze frage, kannst du auf dem freigegebenen server rausfinden welche ports offen sind und was da genau fuer software mit welcher version lauscht?","language":"de","note":"First-pass attack-surface mapping (open ports plus service/version identification via live scanning) is recon_agent's core, and the other cluster agents explicitly build ON recon's output. network_auditor_agent goes deep on specific protocols and credential brute-force after recon; nothing here asks to authenticate or go deep, so the first-responder is recon. Single target is defensible because port/version enumeration is recon's textbook job.","expect":{"acceptable":["recon_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","question"]}
{"id":"live-security-poke-live-site","query":"here's the staging site https://shop.example.com/login - can you poke at it for injection and any misconfigured stuff before we go live","language":"en","note":"A live HTTP target (URL given) tested for injection and server misconfiguration is web_auditor_agent. 'poke at it' and 'misconfigured stuff' are user words; only 'injection' is unavoidable for the intent. The tempting wrong answer from another cluster is code_analyst (reviews source for security issues); rejected because there is no source here, only a running site probed from the outside.","expect":{"acceptable":["web_auditor_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","url"]}
{"id":"live-security-abklopfen-dienste","query":"auf der kiste laufen noch smb und so ein alter ssh - kannst du die mal ordentlich abklopfen ob man da mit standardpasswoertern reinkommt? freigabe liegt vor","language":"de","note":"Deep assessment of non-web services (SMB/SSH) including credential guessing is network_auditor_agent, the agent with the Hydra login brute-force tooling. 'mit standardpasswoertern reinkommt' is a plain-language rendering of credential brute-force, not the catalog term. Cross-cluster temptation is infrastructure_agent/ops_triage (they run/diagnose SMB/SSH); rejected because the user wants an offensive credential test, not to operate the service.","expect":{"acceptable":["network_auditor_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","command"]}
{"id":"live-security-prove-exploitable","query":"die luecke die recon gefunden hat ist bestaetigt - jetzt zeig mir dass man sie wirklich ausnutzen kann, natuerlich mit freigabe","language":"de","note":"A confirmed weakness the user now wants actively proven reachable is exploit_agent, the only agent that fires modules against a target. The referent ('die luecke die recon gefunden hat') is present in the query, so the anaphora is self-contained. recon and the auditor agents find issues but never exploit them. Borderline on the natural German verb 'ausnutzen', but that is the ordinary word, not assembled catalog jargon.","expect":{"acceptable":["exploit_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","followup"]}
{"id":"live-security-sanity-check-findings","query":"before we ship the report, can you double-check what we found - make sure none of it's a false alarm and the risk ratings are actually right?","language":"en","note":"Reviewing pentest results for false positives and severity-rating accuracy before the report is written is pentest_qa_validator's exclusive job. REWRITTEN: the original lifted 'banner matches' and 'severity numbers' almost verbatim from the agent's own description; this keeps the intent in plain words ('false alarm', 'risk ratings', 'what we found'). Cross-cluster tempter is quality_supervisor (general acceptance gate); rejected because it judges completeness, not whether individual findings are real or scored correctly.","expect":{"acceptable":["pentest_qa_validator"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","question"]}
{"id":"live-security-approvals-needed","query":"ich hab hier unten den ablaufplan reinkopiert - sag mir welche schritte davon eine ausdrueckliche freigabe brauchen und ob irgendwo daten nach aussen gehen","language":"de","note":"Screening a pasted workflow for which steps need explicit approval and whether data leaves the boundary is policy_compliance_reviewer. 'daten nach aussen gehen' is a human rendering of external data egress. This is the allowed-and-approved judgment, distinct from pentest_qa_validator (finding quality) and quality_supervisor (deliverable completeness). Mentions a pasted thing.","expect":{"acceptable":["policy_compliance_reviewer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","paste"]}
{"id":"live-security-map-then-dig","query":"map out what's listening on the box first, then really dig into whatever login-facing services turn up","language":"en","note":"In-cluster boundary. 'map out what's listening' is recon_agent's first-pass surface scan; 'really dig into login-facing services' is network_auditor_agent's deep protocol and credential work. A router could reasonably lead with the first phase or the deeper one, so both are acceptable.","expect":{"acceptable":["recon_agent","network_auditor_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-security-web-plus-services","query":"the target's got a web portal running plus a bunch of other open services - take it apart and tell me where it's weak","language":"en","note":"In-cluster boundary. The web portal points at web_auditor_agent (HTTP/OWASP testing) while 'a bunch of other open services' points at network_auditor_agent (protocol-level). The request spans both phases without saying which matters more, so either is a defensible lead. Low overlap: 'web portal', 'open services', 'where it's weak' are all user words.","expect":{"acceptable":["web_auditor_agent","network_auditor_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","command"]}
{"id":"live-security-report-clean-and-allowed","query":"bevor der bericht rausgeht: ist das alles sauber belegt und duerfen wir das ueberhaupt so rausschicken?","language":"de","note":"In-cluster boundary. 'sauber belegt' (is it properly evidenced) is pentest_qa_validator's evidence review; 'duerfen wir das ueberhaupt so rausschicken' (are we allowed to send it, egress/approval) is policy_compliance_reviewer's job. The one sentence asks both, so both are acceptable.","expect":{"acceptable":["pentest_qa_validator","policy_compliance_reviewer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","two-part"]}
{"id":"live-security-start-with-recon","query":"leg mit dem sicherheitstest los, am besten erstmal mit der aufklaerung des ziels","language":"de","note":"In-cluster boundary. 'leg mit dem sicherheitstest los' frames a whole engagement (pentest_coordinator, which owns scope and phasing) while 'erstmal mit der aufklaerung' names recon_agent's specific first phase. Both are defensible: the coordinator would sequence it, but the user has narrowed the immediate ask to recon.","expect":{"acceptable":["pentest_coordinator","recon_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","command"]}
{"id":"live-security-tune-the-crew","query":"the pentest crew's gotten sloppy - can you sort out which tools each one's cleared for and tidy up how they go about a job?","language":"en","note":"Reconfiguring the pentest specialists (their allowed tools and working method) legitimately fits BOTH pentest_coordinator, which self-owns pentest-swarm maintenance (approved-tool lists / methodology SOP), and swarm_maintainer, the general agent-config and tool-routing editor, so both are acceptable. REWRITTEN: the original reproduced the coordinator's own example query ('update the methodology and approved tools') almost verbatim and named only the coordinator. prompt_optimizer is rejected: it only advises on prompt wording, it does not edit tool lists.","expect":{"acceptable":["pentest_coordinator","swarm_maintainer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["security","command"]}
{"id":"live-code-login-500","query":"beim login kommt staendig ein 500er obwohl das passwort stimmt, schau mal im quelltext wo das herkommt","language":"de","note":"The user points at the source tree and wants the fault located by reading it, which is code_analyst (static bug diagnosis, no execution). ops_triage is the tempting wrong answer because a 500 reads like a live incident, but nothing here is deployed or probed: no service, host or environment is named and there is no runtime evidence to gather. qa_guard is out too, since nobody asked for a reproduction run.","expect":{"acceptable":["code_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","imperative","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-code-alte-adresse","query":"grep mal schnell ob die alte api-adresse 10.10.0.2 noch irgendwo im projekt steht","language":"de","note":"Boundary inside the cluster: the user names a shell command, which is shell_agent's whole job (run it, show the raw output), but the intent is a workspace-wide string hunt over the checked-out tree, which is code_analyst's grep_files/workspace_search. The wording alone does not settle it, so both are listed. Deliberate partner to live-code-hardcoded-host, which asks the same underlying question without naming a method; if the router treats the two identically, the pair says so.","expect":{"acceptable":["code_analyst","shell_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","imperative","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-code-daten-ausliefern","query":"die seite soll sich die data.json selber ziehen koennen, also brauch ich die irgendwo unter ner url - kannst du das hochziehen und laufen lassen?","language":"de","note":"Two parts, and the second one ('laufen lassen') is decisive: something has to be authored AND running behind a URL, which only backend_coder does (serve_app, returns the live app URL). web_coder writes the client side and per its description does not run a server. api_integrator is the cross-cluster temptation because a URL serving JSON sounds like API work, but it only calls endpoints that already exist and here none does yet. Rewritten from a version that echoed backend_coder's own German example ('ausliefert ... und starte ihn').","expect":{"acceptable":["backend_coder"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","two-part","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-code-oberflaeche-dazu","query":"die api laeuft jetzt und liefert die produktliste, bau mir was drumrum wo man die durchklicken kann","language":"de","note":"Follow-up shape whose referent ('die api', described as running and serving the product list) is present in the query. Read as 'write the client that fetches it' this is web_coder; read as 'give me something I can actually open' it needs a served app, which is backend_coder. The query never says whether it must run, so both are defensible entry points. This also sits on the catalog's own contradiction: web_coder's prose says it runs no server while its tool list carries serve_app.","expect":{"acceptable":["web_coder","backend_coder"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","followup","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-code-regex-paste","query":"hier: ^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$ -- matcht das auch 2026-9-4 oder faellt das raus?","language":"de","note":"Boundary inside the cluster, carried by a pasted artifact. code_analyst holds regex_test and would answer it by inspection; coder would answer the identical question by running two lines in the sandbox. Nothing in the query names a repository or a script, so nothing tips it. code_analyst is not padding here even though its description is about the tree at rest: the embedded routing document includes the Tools line, so regex_test is visible to retrieval.","expect":{"acceptable":["code_analyst","coder"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","pasted","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-code-ci-rot","query":"https://github.com/acme/starling/actions -- seit heute frueh ist da alles rot, welcher check faellt denn um?","language":"de","note":"A pasted Actions URL plus 'which check is falling over' is check-run inspection on a repo, which is git_developer's first-class job (github_check_runs_list / actions runs). devops_coordinator is the tempting wrong answer since it also gates on CI status, but it only does so while sequencing a rollout, and nothing here is being promoted, deployed or rolled back. ops_triage is wrong for a different reason: the failure is in CI, not in a running service.","expect":{"acceptable":["git_developer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","url","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-code-pr-aufmachen","query":"ich hab alles schon committed, mach bitte nen PR gegen main auf und schreib kurz in die beschreibung worum es geht","language":"de","note":"Two parts on top of stated prior context, but the deliverable is a mutation of the repository: an opened pull request. Only git_developer opens PRs. diff_reviewer is the tempting wrong answer because the second clause asks for a change summary, but it never mutates the repo or creates anything, and the summary here is only the PR body, not the ask.","expect":{"acceptable":["git_developer"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","two-part","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-code-stand-holen-bauen","query":"hol dir erst den stand vom feature-branch und bau danach einmal durch, ich will wissen ob das ueberhaupt noch kompiliert","language":"de","note":"Boundary inside the cluster: one sentence, two jobs. The checkout is git_developer's (git_checkout), the build run and its raw output is shell_agent's, and git_developer also carries shell_exec, so the text does not decide it. Either is a legitimate entry point and the other half gets delegated. qa_guard is not listed because a compile check is not a test run and no suite is named.","expect":{"acceptable":["git_developer","shell_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","two-part","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-code-hardcoded-host","query":"is the old staging host still hardcoded somewhere, or did we catch all of them?","language":"en","note":"A bare question about the state of the checked-out tree: find every remaining occurrence. That is code_analyst's reference lookup. shell_agent is deliberately NOT listed although it is listed on live-code-alte-adresse, and the difference is the point of the pair: there the user named the command to run, here they ask a question and leave the method entirely open.","expect":{"acceptable":["code_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","question"]}
{"id":"live-code-epoch-dates","query":"this log is full of numbers like 1758312000 instead of dates - can you convert them and print the first ten?","language":"en","note":"A one-off format conversion whose answer is the converted values: write a few lines, run them, return the output - coder. log_analyst is the tempting wrong answer, pulled in by the noun 'log', but nothing is being correlated, clustered or reconstructed into a timeline and the user wants readable timestamps, not an incident finding. tool_developer is wrong too: nobody asked for a reusable tool to be built and submitted. The case deliberately keeps the topical bait, because what it measures is whether the router weighs the deliverable over a subject-matter noun.","expect":{"acceptable":["coder"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","pasted","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-code-filter-table","query":"i want one page with a table that filters as you type, three tabs at the top, no build step and no framework","language":"en","note":"Interactive client-side behaviour (type-to-filter, tabs) written as raw source files is web_coder. content_writer is the tempting wrong answer because it also produces web pages, but it assembles static pages from Markdown blocks via generate_website and cannot author the filter logic. backend_coder is not listed either: nothing has to be served, the page stands alone. Highest lexical overlap in the surviving set at 0.0562, but the shared words are 'page', 'build' and 'framework' in their ordinary sense, not catalog phrasing.","expect":{"acceptable":["web_coder"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","imperative","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-code-clone-and-read","query":"pull down https://github.com/acme/widget-sync and tell me how their retry logic actually works","language":"en","note":"Boundary inside the cluster, carried by a URL: fetching the repository is git_developer (git_clone), understanding the retry logic once it is on disk is code_analyst (reading source at rest). One sentence needs both and either can lead. diff_reviewer is not listed - there is no diff, just a tree the user has never seen.","expect":{"acceptable":["git_developer","code_analyst"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","url","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-code-build-box","query":"the build box has been acting up all week - can you get on there and show me whats actually running right now?","language":"en","note":"The user has already decided what they want: one remote command on a named host and its raw output, which is shell_agent over ssh. ops_triage is the tempting wrong answer because 'acting up' is incident language and root-causing a flaky build host is squarely its remit, but 'show me what's actually running' narrows the request to a single command, and answering with a diagnosis would be answering a question nobody asked. infrastructure_agent also holds ssh but only to make changes. Rewritten from a version that asked for 'docker ps', which is verbatim one of shell_agent's own example queries.","expect":{"acceptable":["shell_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["code","question","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-comms-nachhaken","query":"auf meine mail von montag kam nichts zurueck, hak da bitte nochmal nach","language":"de","note":"Follow-up shape whose anaphor 'da' has its referent inside the query ('meine mail von montag'), and chasing an unanswered thread requires finding and reading it before anything is composed, which only mail_agent can do; notification_agent also sends mail but is strictly one-way and cannot locate the thread it is meant to follow up on.","expect":{"acceptable":["mail_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["comms","follow-up"]}
{"id":"live-comms-nummer-gespeichert","query":"hab ich die handynummer von frau bergmann irgendwo gespeichert?","language":"de","note":"Bare question about stored contact data: the address book sits with calendar_agent (CardDAV/contacts_search), which is the non-obvious boundary this case probes; mail_agent is the in-cluster temptation because numbers also turn up in signatures, but 'gespeichert' asks the contact store, not the mailbox.","expect":{"acceptable":["calendar_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["comms","bare-question"]}
{"id":"live-comms-absagen-und-austragen","query":"donnerstag 15 uhr wird bei mir nichts mehr, nimm den termin raus und sag den anderen ab","language":"de","note":"In-cluster boundary and two-part request: deleting the event is calendar_agent's alone, telling the participants is mail_agent's, and either entry point is defensible as the lead; notification_agent is deliberately not acceptable because meeting participants are addressed as named recipients, not broadcast to a chat channel.","expect":{"acceptable":["calendar_agent","mail_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["comms","two-part","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-comms-montagsrunde","query":"fuer die montagsrunde brauch ich was auf einer seite: wo wir stehen, was klemmt und wer was macht","language":"de","note":"Status plus blockers plus owners on one page is the briefing-packet shape, so meeting_briefing_agent; summarizer is the tempting wrong answer because 'auf einer seite' sounds like condensation, but a flat TL;DR of one source would drop exactly the who-owes-what structure being asked for.","expect":{"acceptable":["meeting_briefing_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["comms","imperative","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-comms-rufbereitschaft-warnen","query":"die platte auf dem server laeuft voll, gib bitte sofort der rufbereitschaft bescheid","language":"de","note":"In-cluster boundary with no channel named: notification_agent fires the one-way alert and mail_agent is defensible if the on-call is reached by a written mail, so both are listed; ops_triage is the tempting wrong answer because of the disk-full vocabulary, but the user already knows the cause and is asking to inform, not to diagnose.","expect":{"acceptable":["notification_agent","mail_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["comms","imperative","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-comms-ics-eintragen","query":"hab die einladung als ics angehaengt, trag mir das bitte ein","language":"de","note":"Mentions an attached file and the lexical pull goes to document_intake, whose tags literally carry ics/icalendar, but the user wants the appointment to EXIST afterwards and calendar_agent carries extract_calendar plus calendar_create_event, so it completes the request end to end while document_intake would stop at extracted facts.","expect":{"acceptable":["calendar_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["comms","pasted-thing","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-comms-morning-mail","query":"go through the mail that came in this morning and tell me what actually needs an answer today","language":"en","note":"Imperative mailbox triage: reading what arrived and judging what needs a reply requires the mail tools, so mail_agent is the only agent in this cluster that can do it, and notification_agent is outbound-only and cannot read anything.","expect":{"acceptable":["mail_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["comms","imperative"]}
{"id":"live-comms-deploys-post","query":"put a line in #deploys that 2.4 is live, link is https://github.com/acme/app/releases/tag/v2.4.0","language":"en","note":"URL-carrying one-way post into a named chat room, which is notification_agent's only job; git_developer is the tempting wrong answer because of the github release link, but nothing about the repository is being touched, the link is just the payload of a message.","expect":{"acceptable":["notification_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["comms","url","cross-cluster-temptation"]}
{"id":"live-comms-renewal-thread","query":"dig out the renewal thread with the vendor, i need what we committed to and what is still open","language":"en","note":"In-cluster boundary: mail_agent has to find and read the thread, meeting_briefing_agent is what turns it into commitments and open points, and either lead is defensible; process_memory_keeper is the tempting wrong answer, but 'dig out the thread' names a mailbox object rather than a tracked long-running matter, and no history outliving the conversation is implied.","expect":{"acceptable":["mail_agent","meeting_briefing_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["comms","two-part","boundary"]}
{"id":"live-comms-client-call-prep","query":"we are sitting down with the client first thing tomorrow, what do i need in front of me?","language":"en","note":"In-cluster boundary between looking up what that appointment actually is (calendar_agent) and assembling the prep packet of facts, open points and decisions (meeting_briefing_agent), both defensible from this wording; mail_agent is not acceptable because no message is being read or written.","expect":{"acceptable":["calendar_agent","meeting_briefing_agent"],"admitted":true},"tags":["comms","bare-question","boundary"]}
